WEBVTT

00:02.413 --> 00:05.315
<i>It seems today that all you see</i>

00:05.550 --> 00:08.849
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:09.121 --> 00:12.489
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:12.592 --> 00:15.255
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:15.763 --> 00:18.288
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:19.066 --> 00:22.059
<i>Lucky there's a man who
positively can do</i>

00:22.504 --> 00:23.971
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:24.072 --> 00:25.472
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:25.808 --> 00:30.678
<i>He's a family guy</i>

00:43.328 --> 00:46.196
<i>The annual Quahog Star Trek convention,
where once a year,</i>

00:46.299 --> 00:49.098
sci-fi buffs take their lips off
the barrel of a loaded gun

00:49.203 --> 00:51.433
and spend half a day
adjusting their eyes to sunlight.

00:55.143 --> 00:57.338
Brian, look.
I purchased authentic blueprints

00:57.445 --> 00:59.346
<i>to build a Star Trek transporter.</i>

00:59.448 --> 01:02.315
Well, that's great, Stewie. You should get
William Shatner to sign them for you.

01:02.418 --> 01:04.819
No way.
I'm getting Patrick Stewart to sign it.

01:04.922 --> 01:06.549
Picard has it all over Kirk.

01:06.657 --> 01:09.491
He's poised and measured
and doesn't wear a cheap rug.

01:09.594 --> 01:12.962
Rather, he accepts even baldness
with a quiet cool that says,

01:13.199 --> 01:17.466
"I am in command. You are safe with me.
I will cradle you in my arms

01:17.571 --> 01:19.698
"through any crisis in any galaxy. "

01:20.440 --> 01:22.136
- Are you queer?
- Probably.

01:22.510 --> 01:25.172
Dad, this is stupid. I'm so bored.

01:25.346 --> 01:27.679
How can you be bored?
This convention has everything.

01:27.783 --> 01:30.149
You can even try on LeVar Burton's VISOR.

01:34.939 --> 01:38.876
Why would he wear these?
Who would invent these for him?

01:41.614 --> 01:46.917
<i>And in conclusion, whether your dreams
are earthbound or set in the stars,</i>

01:47.054 --> 01:50.217
<i>follow your heart and make it so.</i>

01:52.961 --> 01:54.792
He said the thing he says on TV!

01:54.896 --> 01:58.389
<i>Now the cast and I would be happy
to answer a few questions.</i>

01:58.634 --> 01:59.862
Yes, so many questions!

01:59.969 --> 02:03.872
Me! Me! Mr. Stewart! Mr. Stewart!
Mr. Stewart! Mr. Stewart!

02:04.140 --> 02:06.439
Stu! Stu! Stu!

02:08.779 --> 02:09.746
<i>Yes, you there.</i>

02:10.949 --> 02:12.211
Yes, I have a question.

02:12.317 --> 02:16.311
Oftentimes my household sponges
accumulate an awful amount of buildup.

02:16.689 --> 02:17.951
What can I do to prevent this?

02:18.057 --> 02:19.615
<i>That's an excellent question.</i>

02:19.726 --> 02:24.255
<i>It's very important to thoroughly
wring out your sponges after every usage.</i>

02:24.465 --> 02:27.526
<i>This will prevent the accumulation
of grime and bacteria.</i>

02:27.636 --> 02:29.730
<i>A dry sponge is a happy sponge.</i>

02:29.905 --> 02:31.600
<i>That's not a Star Trek question.</i>

02:31.707 --> 02:33.641
I have a question for Jonathan Frakes.

02:33.743 --> 02:35.678
I have this itch on the back of my leg,

02:35.779 --> 02:38.270
and I can't figure out
if it's a bug bite or dry skin.

02:38.382 --> 02:40.010
<i>- Do you take hot showers?
- Yes.</i>

02:40.118 --> 02:41.415
<i>- Dry skin.
- Thanks.</i>

02:41.519 --> 02:43.646
<i>These aren't Star Trek questions.
What the hell?</i>

02:43.755 --> 02:45.587
I have a question for Gates McFadden.

02:45.691 --> 02:47.591
I've got an artesian well on my property

02:47.693 --> 02:50.288
and the water pressure is lousy.
Any suggestions?

02:50.397 --> 02:53.230
<i>I would check the point first
before re-priming it.</i>

02:53.366 --> 02:55.631
<i>But remember that the summer months
take a particular toll</i>

02:55.736 --> 02:58.364
<i>on any region's aquifer,
depending on the local climate.</i>

02:58.472 --> 02:59.462
This is horse shit!

02:59.574 --> 03:03.944
<i>And that's the last question. Thank you
for coming. You've been wonderful.</i>

03:06.582 --> 03:08.049
You bastards!

03:08.284 --> 03:10.276
I'll get my question answered
one way or another.

03:10.521 --> 03:13.685
All I'm saying is that in the episode
"Relics," when Scotty rematerialized

03:13.792 --> 03:16.784
<i>on the Jenolen,
he referenced Captain Kirk still being alive,</i>

03:16.895 --> 03:19.228
which is ridiculous
because he knew he watched him die

03:19.331 --> 03:21.299
<i>on the Enterprise B
Generations.</i>

03:21.400 --> 03:23.096
There's a perfectly simple explanation.

03:23.203 --> 03:26.331
He was caught in
a transporter pattern buffer for 75 years

03:26.440 --> 03:30.036
and Riker mentioned a 0.003%
signal degradation,

03:30.144 --> 03:32.442
which would account
for Scotty's memory loss.

03:32.548 --> 03:35.278
Well, well, look what
we have here, Jonathan.

03:35.384 --> 03:38.843
Yup, looks like we got ourselves
a couple of nerds.

03:42.993 --> 03:44.460
Give me $6.

03:46.163 --> 03:48.758
Oh, my God! What a great costume. Meg.

03:48.900 --> 03:51.130
Meg, come take your picture
with this space-alien guy.

03:51.236 --> 03:53.569
- No, Dad. I don't want to.
- Come on. It'll be funny.

03:57.305 --> 03:59.933
What a wonderful novelty photo
this will make.

04:00.041 --> 04:02.772
Thanks so much, buddy.
Hey, how'd you make that awesome mask?

04:02.878 --> 04:05.108
It's not a mask. I have the mumps.

04:05.348 --> 04:08.284
<i>What? You came to a Star Trek
convention with the mumps?</i>

04:08.385 --> 04:10.512
You could be infecting people
with the disease.

04:10.620 --> 04:14.057
Yeah, like that old gypsy did to
Britney Spears in that Stephen King book.

04:14.525 --> 04:16.084
Thicker!

04:19.898 --> 04:23.300
Well, Meg has the mumps all right.
How is it she was never immunized?

04:23.403 --> 04:26.134
Well, it was 1992 and I couldn't
be bothered with anything

04:26.240 --> 04:28.902
that didn't involve Dan Cortese.
Besides, what's the big deal?

04:29.009 --> 04:30.910
- I never got a mumps shot.
- Really?

04:31.012 --> 04:33.071
Well, I'd caution you
that getting the mumps as an adult

04:33.181 --> 04:35.081
could result in serious complications.

04:35.183 --> 04:38.176
In some cases, the symptoms
could spread to the testicular glands.

04:38.287 --> 04:39.618
Big deal. So I'll wear socks.

04:39.722 --> 04:41.850
Mr. Griffin, your testicles
are not in your feet.

04:41.959 --> 04:43.859
- Well, where are they?
- Under your penis.

04:43.961 --> 04:46.453
Are you kidding? I always thought
those were two little sandbags

04:46.564 --> 04:48.691
to keep flood waters
from floating into my bum.

04:48.800 --> 04:52.601
No. No, I'm just poking
at your funny bone. I am quite alarmed.

04:52.705 --> 04:54.697
I don't think you realize the danger.

04:54.808 --> 04:57.606
Like the people who think it's okay
to bring shampoo on an airplane.

04:57.978 --> 05:02.040
So I told Brenda, "I work hard.
I like a clean house when I come home. "

05:02.183 --> 05:03.775
And now I'm the bad guy.

05:03.885 --> 05:05.717
Oh, I know exactly where you're coming...

05:05.821 --> 05:07.311
Ow! It's in my eyes!

05:13.696 --> 05:16.632
See, Chris, come here.
Come here, look. Check it out.

05:17.935 --> 05:19.403
Holy crap! No way!

05:20.605 --> 05:22.368
I know, huh? Classic.

05:23.543 --> 05:25.135
I got to forward this to my bud.

05:31.418 --> 05:33.944
Meg, I know you hate having to be
in bed all day.

05:34.055 --> 05:36.455
But your father's bringing in the old TV.

05:36.558 --> 05:38.993
- Hey, Meg.
- Peter, what the hell?

05:39.094 --> 05:41.619
I don't want to catch the mumps, Lois.
Here's your TV, Meg.

05:41.730 --> 05:43.096
It's a little old and there's no remote

05:43.200 --> 05:46.863
and it only gets one channel
and it's not on that channel right now.

05:47.504 --> 05:49.871
<i>Chris, check it out. Jackass Number Two.</i>

06:04.558 --> 06:07.551
This whole day has been
one big laugh riot.

06:12.537 --> 06:14.903
<i>- Finally!
Up next, Kirk Cameron...</i>

06:15.007 --> 06:15.974
Ooh!

06:16.074 --> 06:18.270
<i>...to talk about God.
- Oh.</i>

06:18.378 --> 06:21.313
<i>Hi. Welcome to the Religion Channel's
number one show,</i>

06:21.414 --> 06:23.110
Kirk and the Lord, Just Hanging.

06:23.217 --> 06:24.775
<i>With me, Kirk Cameron.</i>

06:25.052 --> 06:28.819
<i>Today, I'm gonna tell you why God
will always be there for you,</i>

06:28.923 --> 06:30.356
<i>even in the worst of times.</i>

06:30.458 --> 06:31.585
No, thanks.

06:31.694 --> 06:36.462
<i>But first, are you lonely, picked on,
unappreciated, disliked,</i>

06:36.700 --> 06:39.260
<i>not totally happy
with your physical appearance?</i>

06:39.369 --> 06:41.395
<i>- Go on.
- Are you unloved?</i>

06:41.706 --> 06:43.970
<i>Do you feel like no one cares about you?</i>

06:44.075 --> 06:47.512
Meg, your mother made soup for you.
Here you go, honey.

06:50.315 --> 06:53.012
<i>Well, you know who does love you?
The Lord.</i>

06:54.087 --> 06:55.419
Here's your milk.

06:59.794 --> 07:02.025
Rupert, my transporter is complete.

07:02.197 --> 07:05.463
<i>If my calculations are correct, the
The Next Generation</i>

07:05.568 --> 07:07.729
will soon be here to answer
all my questions.

07:10.307 --> 07:11.467
Wait a minute. Something's wrong.

07:13.744 --> 07:15.076
All right, you girls ready?

07:16.548 --> 07:17.515
What's going on?

07:18.683 --> 07:19.742
Don't you laugh at it.

07:26.326 --> 07:27.520
Good morning, Mom and Dad.

07:27.627 --> 07:30.825
Wow! Look who's finally out of her room
after five days.

07:31.132 --> 07:34.830
Oh, you're alive. I guess
you are gonna need that college fund.

07:34.937 --> 07:36.302
Chris, do Daddy a favor.

07:36.405 --> 07:39.307
In the garage,
there is a very expensive show camel.

07:39.576 --> 07:41.840
Please return him to the bazaar
for a refund.

07:41.945 --> 07:44.938
- We have to give away Humpy?
- I told you not to name him.

07:45.049 --> 07:47.574
- So, you feel better, Meg?
- All better, Mom.

07:47.718 --> 07:49.846
I was made well by the hand of God.

07:49.988 --> 07:54.449
"This is the day that the Lord hath made.
Let us rejoice and be glad in it. "

07:54.594 --> 07:55.993
Meg, what are you talking about?

07:56.095 --> 07:59.554
I'm talking about God, Mom.
I've been reborn.

07:59.900 --> 08:01.891
That's right, folks.
It's gonna be a Meg episode.

08:02.002 --> 08:03.630
Stick around for the fun.

08:05.173 --> 08:07.734
Here's the clicker.
No one would blame you.

08:13.884 --> 08:15.749
What do you mean you found the Lord?

08:15.852 --> 08:17.878
I've been washed in the blood of the lamb.

08:17.989 --> 08:21.891
Kirk Cameron explained it all to me.
The Lord is my savior.

08:22.026 --> 08:23.585
It's that damn religion channel.

08:23.695 --> 08:25.686
She was watching it all day
while she was bedridden.

08:25.797 --> 08:27.993
I want to share the word of God
with everyone I know,

08:28.101 --> 08:29.625
starting with my family.

08:29.736 --> 08:31.397
Now, everyone hold hands,

08:31.571 --> 08:33.802
because we're gonna say grace
before we eat.

08:33.908 --> 08:36.001
Dad, would you like to do the honors?

08:36.110 --> 08:38.579
Are you kidding?
I'd love a chance to shine.

08:38.680 --> 08:40.477
All right, Peter, this is it.

08:40.949 --> 08:44.716
<i>Dear Lord, please give me the cheat
codes for Mike Tyson's Punch-Out!</i>

08:44.854 --> 08:47.585
I have been stuck on Bald Bull
for four years.

08:47.691 --> 08:51.651
I tried left, left, up, B, dodge,
uppercut, but he still knocks me out.

08:51.996 --> 08:53.327
And, you know, they say
you're supposed to go

08:53.431 --> 08:55.399
right, B, up, dodge, left, uppercut...

08:55.500 --> 08:58.061
Listen to me telling you
how to play the game.

08:58.170 --> 09:01.470
Hey, you want to see a sweet porn
website? Follow me upstairs.

09:03.543 --> 09:05.808
I know what you're thinking,
"Whoever heard of an erotic Chinese?"

09:05.913 --> 09:06.937
But there it is.

09:12.120 --> 09:13.553
All right. Let's try this again.

09:19.329 --> 09:20.558
It's them! I did it!

09:20.664 --> 09:23.861
<i>The Next Generation
is here to answer my questions.</i>

09:23.968 --> 09:25.436
What the hell? Where am I?

09:25.537 --> 09:26.663
What's going on?

09:26.771 --> 09:29.239
Greetings, everyone.
My name is Stewie Griffin.

09:29.341 --> 09:31.674
I've transported you all here
against your will.

09:31.777 --> 09:34.770
I'm a huge fan, and you're going to answer
all my questions.

09:34.881 --> 09:38.112
- But you're a baby.
- Yes. That's right, Denise Crosby.

09:39.854 --> 09:43.312
That was a warning. Please do not speak
unless you're spoken to.

09:43.424 --> 09:45.086
Now, question number one.

09:45.327 --> 09:48.819
- What's it like on the set?
- The show's been off the air for 15 years.

09:48.931 --> 09:51.162
Although I will say
it was an awful lot of fun.

09:51.268 --> 09:53.566
You know, when Patrick
wasn't hogging the limelight.

09:53.670 --> 09:57.402
Oh, fuck you, Michael! Fifteen years later
you've still got that attitude.

09:57.541 --> 10:00.443
Oh, my God,
I am already having a fantastic time.

10:00.545 --> 10:04.482
- Ooh! Hey, let's spend the day together.
- Hey, that sounds like fun. Ow!

10:04.584 --> 10:06.745
- Shut up, Wil.
- Stop it, Patrick.

10:06.853 --> 10:08.981
You know, I think you should all be nicer
to Whil Wheaton.

10:09.089 --> 10:11.580
The way I treat my colleagues...
Wait, what?

10:11.692 --> 10:13.456
I said you ought to be nicer
to Whil Wheaton.

10:13.561 --> 10:15.256
- You mean Wil Wheaton?
- Yes, Whil Wheaton.

10:15.363 --> 10:16.352
Why are you saying it like that?

10:16.464 --> 10:18.092
What? I'm just saying you should be nicer
to Whil Wheaton.

10:18.200 --> 10:19.565
Whil Wheaton seems like a nice guy.

10:19.669 --> 10:21.136
- Say "wheat. "
- Wheat.

10:21.270 --> 10:23.296
- Now say "Wil Wheaton. "
- Whil Wheaton.

10:23.407 --> 10:24.533
- Wil Wheaton.
- Whil Wheaton.

10:24.641 --> 10:25.869
- Wil Wheaton.
- Whil Wheaton.

10:25.976 --> 10:27.170
- Wil Wheaton.
- Whil Wheaton.

10:27.277 --> 10:28.745
- Wil Wheaton.
- Hey, did you hook up

10:28.846 --> 10:31.212
- with Whoopi Goldberg on the show?
- All the time.

10:33.550 --> 10:34.778
Meg, what the hell? I was watching that.

10:34.884 --> 10:36.351
It's time for Kirk Cameron.

10:36.453 --> 10:39.821
And I think it's important for all of you
to hear his inspiring message

10:39.924 --> 10:42.519
- about the word of God.
- Again, Meg?

10:42.627 --> 10:45.221
You know, I think it's wonderful
you found something to have faith in,

10:45.330 --> 10:47.196
but there's such a thing as moderation.

10:47.300 --> 10:49.700
Mom, you sound like a nonbeliever.

10:50.002 --> 10:51.971
Brian, you're a thoughtful person.

10:52.072 --> 10:54.802
Are you willing to open yourself up
to God's truth?

10:54.908 --> 10:57.309
You're barking up the wrong tree, Meg.
I'm an atheist.

10:58.480 --> 11:01.244
- What's that?
- I don't believe in God.

11:01.784 --> 11:06.882
- What? Brian, how can you say that?
- Why, I just thought you knew.

11:06.990 --> 11:09.720
I mean, I never go to church.
You know how I feel about that.

11:09.826 --> 11:12.762
No. Brian, it's one thing to bash
organized religion,

11:12.864 --> 11:16.926
but we believe in God in this house.
I mean, an atheist?

11:17.102 --> 11:19.468
That's just about the worst thing
a person can be.

11:19.571 --> 11:22.473
You're not gonna get anything
for Christmas, Brian.

11:22.575 --> 11:24.702
- Guys, I'm just trying to say...
- Shut up, beast.

11:24.811 --> 11:28.145
I have dominion over you.
And I command you to believe in God.

11:28.249 --> 11:30.616
I'm sorry. I just don't see any evidence.

11:30.719 --> 11:32.380
I mean, look at the Hubble Telescope.

11:32.487 --> 11:36.083
It's discovered untold wonders
of a vast, unexplored universe,

11:36.192 --> 11:39.525
but not one picture of a guy with a beard
sitting around on a cloud.

11:39.629 --> 11:40.756
I mean, what's he doing up there?

11:48.606 --> 11:51.041
You know, you keep talking like that,
God's gonna get you, Brian.

11:51.143 --> 11:53.008
He's gonna get you with the Kodak Disc.

11:53.112 --> 11:55.604
<i>Oh, God's gonna get you
with the Kodak Disc</i>

11:56.583 --> 11:57.948
I'm sorry. What were we talking about?

12:02.757 --> 12:04.817
Hey, where the hell is my van?

12:08.079 --> 12:10.810
Stewie, I'm not really
much of a fast-food eater.

12:10.916 --> 12:13.316
Yeah? Can you read my mind?
Can you tell what I'm thinking right now?

12:13.418 --> 12:14.909
I'm thinking, "Shut up and get a salad. "

12:15.021 --> 12:17.387
- I want some McNuggets.
- We'll get to you, Brent.

12:17.490 --> 12:22.190
I want a hamburger. No, a cheeseburger.
I want a hot dog. I want a milkshake...

12:22.296 --> 12:23.924
You'll get nothing and like it.

12:24.032 --> 12:25.966
<i>- Uh, hello?
Yes. Welcome to McDonald's.</i>

12:26.067 --> 12:28.092
<i>- Can I help you?
- Hailing frequencies open, huh?</i>

12:28.203 --> 12:29.796
Okay. Yeah.

12:29.906 --> 12:33.000
We're gonna get two McChicken
sandwiches, and a Diet Coke.

12:33.109 --> 12:36.079
- And what do you want, Michael?
- A McDLT.

12:36.179 --> 12:38.375
No. I already told you
they don't make those anymore.

12:38.483 --> 12:41.111
You know, sometimes it's a regional thing.
You could ask.

12:41.219 --> 12:44.053
No McDonald's anywhere
makes a McDLT anymore.

12:44.156 --> 12:46.056
I'd love a Shamrock Shake,
if they've got any of those.

12:46.158 --> 12:47.455
It's September, Jonathan.

12:47.560 --> 12:49.825
Stewie, can I take this
goddamn headband off?

12:49.930 --> 12:52.125
No, LeVar. You're blind.
That's the only way you can see.

12:52.232 --> 12:54.565
I'm just saying they have
all the ingredients for a...

12:55.736 --> 12:57.500
Just hang on, all right?
There's a lot of us in...

12:57.606 --> 12:59.233
There's a lot of... It's a big order.

12:59.341 --> 13:02.105
- What time do they stop serving breakfast?
- It's 3:00.

13:02.210 --> 13:05.374
- Some of them serve breakfast all day.
- None of them serve breakfast all day.

13:05.481 --> 13:06.505
Do they have beer?

13:09.386 --> 13:10.353
Hey, Brian.

13:10.454 --> 13:12.423
In hopes that you'll open your heart
to God,

13:12.524 --> 13:14.048
I wanted to give you this cross.

13:14.159 --> 13:15.456
No, I don't want a crucifix.

13:15.560 --> 13:18.052
Would you want it if I threw it over there?

13:18.164 --> 13:19.153
No. Please don't do that.

13:19.265 --> 13:21.096
- You gonna get it, boy?
- No. Please, no.

13:21.200 --> 13:22.190
Go get it, boy.

13:26.173 --> 13:28.142
Okay. I'll take Jesus back now.

13:51.458 --> 13:54.291
Brian, Kirk Cameron
is the one who converted me.

13:54.427 --> 13:56.692
But unfortunately he's not available.

13:56.831 --> 13:59.265
<i>So I got his younger brother
from Growing Pains.</i>

13:59.367 --> 14:01.700
Will you guys buy me a case of Sudafed?

14:01.803 --> 14:03.737
Don't you want to tell Brian about Jesus?

14:03.839 --> 14:07.867
They got my picture up at the drugstore
and they won't sell me any Sudafed.

14:08.044 --> 14:09.841
I'll make it worth your while.

14:09.947 --> 14:11.471
- Ben.
- Dad.

14:11.582 --> 14:16.611
Ben, what have I told you about trading
sexual favors for Sudafed?

14:17.188 --> 14:19.657
Look, Meg, I've had enough of this.
You're not gonna convert me.

14:19.759 --> 14:23.092
But, Brian, I just want you to feel the joy
that I feel.

14:23.195 --> 14:25.858
I mean, the church makes me feel
accepted and safe

14:25.966 --> 14:28.093
and part of something bigger than myself.

14:28.201 --> 14:31.365
But, Meg, you don't need
an outside voice to feel those feelings.

14:31.472 --> 14:32.734
They're inside you.

14:32.840 --> 14:35.332
What you call God is inside you, all of us.

14:35.611 --> 14:38.102
And I just hate to see people
hating and killing each other

14:38.213 --> 14:41.377
over their own interpretation of what
they're not smart enough to understand.

14:41.484 --> 14:43.953
- You see what I'm saying?
- Oh, I do, Brian.

14:44.088 --> 14:46.113
And I think I know just what to do.

14:46.457 --> 14:48.892
Good evening. I'm Tom Tucker.
Our top story tonight:

14:48.994 --> 14:51.360
Just when you thought the world
couldn't be any more dangerous,

14:51.463 --> 14:55.230
Channel Five News has discovered
that there is an atheist among us.

14:55.334 --> 14:58.236
Local churchgoer and junior
Christian soldier Meg Griffin

14:58.338 --> 15:01.705
has identified the atheist as Brian Griffin
of Spooner Street.

15:01.875 --> 15:03.537
Here's the reaction from city hall.

15:03.845 --> 15:05.870
Shocking to say the least.

15:06.181 --> 15:08.878
I'd rather have a terrorist
living in our midst.

15:09.018 --> 15:13.547
At least they believe in a God,
even if it's a smelly brown God.

15:14.024 --> 15:16.492
Meg, how the hell could you do
something like this?

15:16.593 --> 15:19.085
If a man hath ears, let him hear, Brian.

15:19.263 --> 15:21.026
All right, what's...
What's the worst that could happen?

15:21.132 --> 15:23.431
This is the 21st century.
People are tolerant.

15:25.137 --> 15:28.505
Well, this is nothing.
Probably just a random act of violence.

15:30.376 --> 15:33.278
I thought only he without sin
could cast the first Prius.

15:43.858 --> 15:45.792
Oh, my God! That was a close one.

15:45.894 --> 15:48.329
- Brian, what happened?
- I'm a pariah, Lois.

15:48.631 --> 15:50.326
Ever since Meg told everyone
I'm an atheist,

15:50.433 --> 15:52.459
I'm the most hated person in town.

15:52.569 --> 15:54.264
I tried to rent a movie
and they threw me out.

15:54.371 --> 15:56.636
I tried to buy a pack of cigarettes
and they threw me out.

15:56.741 --> 15:59.801
But the most serious part of it is
no bar would serve me a drink.

15:59.911 --> 16:01.573
I'm starting to get pretty desperate.

16:01.680 --> 16:04.012
Okay, just remember to act confident.
You're gonna do great.

16:04.116 --> 16:05.812
You look real grown up.

16:06.419 --> 16:09.013
Uh, yes,
I'd like to buy some alcohol, please.

16:09.355 --> 16:12.382
- Okay, can I see your ID?
- I don't have one.

16:12.760 --> 16:14.887
- You don't?
- No, it's me, Chris.

16:15.362 --> 16:18.924
- Oh, hey, Chris.
- Hey, Carl. Can I buy some alcohol?

16:19.101 --> 16:20.899
- No.
- Oh, okay.

16:21.471 --> 16:24.201
<i>- Hey, you know what's a great movie?
- The Reaping?</i>

16:24.307 --> 16:27.402
Yeah. Why are you dressed
like John Lithgow?

16:28.112 --> 16:31.549
Well, if you ask me, I think laying off
the sauce could do you some good, Brian.

16:31.649 --> 16:33.947
Yeah, right.
If you need me, I'll be in the kitchen.

16:35.743 --> 16:38.177
I hope he finds faith of some kind.

16:38.279 --> 16:40.874
You know who doesn't have
all these problems? Marmaduke.

16:40.983 --> 16:43.178
All he does is eat pies off the high counter.

16:43.285 --> 16:46.551
Next time around, we're gonna get
ourselves a big, tall, pie-eating dog, Lois.

16:46.656 --> 16:49.592
- Okay, Peter.
- Or Howard Huge. Let's get Howard Huge.

16:49.994 --> 16:51.757
Great. We have a game plan.

17:01.941 --> 17:04.035
Hold it together, Brian. Hold it together.

17:04.144 --> 17:06.271
Come on. You know you want a drink.

17:06.380 --> 17:08.747
Yeah, come on, Brian, drink us.

17:08.850 --> 17:11.819
Come on, drink me.
What are you waiting for?

17:11.920 --> 17:13.513
Yeah, you big silly ass.

17:13.622 --> 17:16.284
Just wrap your lips around me
and take a big gulp.

17:16.392 --> 17:17.916
Get to the chopper.

17:26.054 --> 17:27.043
All right, everybody got
your bowling shoes?

17:27.155 --> 17:29.317
- Everybody got your balls?
- I don't have my shoes.

17:29.425 --> 17:31.985
Jonathan, we were just up at the counter.
Why didn't you get your shoes?

17:32.095 --> 17:33.791
- I don't have my shoes, either.
- What the hell?

17:33.897 --> 17:35.296
You need your shoes to bowl.

17:35.399 --> 17:37.800
Now, why exactly can I not wear
my loafers?

17:37.902 --> 17:39.130
What is the danger there?

17:39.237 --> 17:42.605
Because, Patrick...
Because, Patrick, those are the rules.

17:42.708 --> 17:46.337
Well, I think it's just because
they want another $1.50 from me.

17:46.445 --> 17:47.913
All right, I'm putting our names in.

17:48.015 --> 17:49.607
- Brent.
- No, no. Don't put Brent.

17:50.784 --> 17:52.309
Put Rock Kickass.

17:52.453 --> 17:54.114
I don't know how to change it.
I already typed it in.

17:54.222 --> 17:55.280
For mine, put Dirk Diggler.

17:55.390 --> 17:57.154
I'm not gonna put everyone
as a fake name.

17:57.259 --> 17:58.487
How do you want to do the teams?

17:58.594 --> 18:00.459
How about the white guys
against the black guys?

18:00.562 --> 18:01.689
Patrick, don't be an instigator.

18:01.798 --> 18:03.459
- I have to pee.
- Brent, take Michael

18:03.566 --> 18:05.534
- to the bathroom, please.
- Okay.

18:07.805 --> 18:10.137
Look at me. I've got girl boobs.

18:19.018 --> 18:22.113
Hey, Meg, guess what? I've seen the light.

18:22.222 --> 18:23.280
- Really?
- Yes.

18:23.390 --> 18:26.690
Hallelujah! I believe in God!
Lordy, Lordy, I believe!

18:27.362 --> 18:30.490
- Brian, that's fantastic news.
- I know. I know.

18:30.598 --> 18:32.624
Hey, you mind spreading the news
around town?

18:32.735 --> 18:35.933
Say maybe down at the liquor store?
Maybe down at The Clam?

18:36.039 --> 18:38.803
Of course, Brian.
But first we have work to do.

18:39.142 --> 18:42.169
God's work. And God will be happy
that you're joining me.

18:42.280 --> 18:45.478
Then I say let's celebrate the way
they did in the Bible. With wine, red wine.

18:45.584 --> 18:46.551
You know, like Jesus drank.

18:48.634 --> 18:51.195
- Do you like the wine?
- Very much. What is it?

18:51.305 --> 18:52.533
It's my blood.

18:53.307 --> 18:56.277
- I have to leave.
- Nah, sit down.

18:59.878 --> 19:02.312
Thanks for setting
everyone straight, Meg.

19:02.413 --> 19:07.181
I feel the warm, healing, liquid presence
of God's genuine, cold-filtered grace.

19:07.286 --> 19:08.913
It was my pleasure, Brian.

19:09.021 --> 19:11.582
And now we get to do the work
of the Lord.

19:12.492 --> 19:14.154
- Come on.
- What? What are we doing?

19:14.262 --> 19:15.786
God's will, Brian.

19:19.635 --> 19:22.297
- A book burning?
- Come on. Grab an armful.

19:22.404 --> 19:25.203
We have to destroy everything
that's harmful to God.

19:31.448 --> 19:33.883
Meg, I can't be a part of this.
And neither should you.

19:33.985 --> 19:37.011
What are you talking about?
I thought you'd seen the light, Brian.

19:37.122 --> 19:40.024
Well, to be honest, I lied for booze.
But, Meg, you're a smart girl.

19:40.126 --> 19:42.492
You ought to be able to see
that what's going on here is wrong.

19:42.595 --> 19:45.258
You are not gonna turn me
from my faith, Brian.

19:47.067 --> 19:49.468
Okay, fine. Then let me just ask you this.

19:49.571 --> 19:51.038
If there were a God,

19:51.172 --> 19:54.574
would he have put you here on Earth
with a flat chest and a fat ass?

19:54.677 --> 19:57.806
- I'm made in his image.
- Really?

19:58.248 --> 20:00.216
Would he give you a smoking hot mom
like Lois

20:00.317 --> 20:02.308
and then have you grow up
looking like Peter?

20:02.420 --> 20:03.387
Well...

20:03.487 --> 20:05.352
And what kind of God
would put you in a house

20:05.456 --> 20:07.391
where no one respects or cares about you,

20:07.492 --> 20:10.017
not even enough to get you
a damn mumps shot?

20:10.862 --> 20:15.926
Oh, no! You're right, Brian. You're right.

20:16.135 --> 20:17.296
I'm sorry, Meg.

20:17.404 --> 20:19.895
But what is there to believe in
without God?

20:20.140 --> 20:21.802
Where do the answers come from?

20:21.910 --> 20:23.844
Well, that's all part
of the human experience.

20:23.945 --> 20:25.845
It's what we're here to find out.

20:25.947 --> 20:28.815
And I bet you that the real answer
to the nature of our existence

20:28.918 --> 20:32.821
is gonna be more unimaginably amazing
than we can possibly conceive.

21:35.432 --> 21:38.697
Rob? Did you hear that?

21:40.171 --> 21:41.195
Hear what?

21:41.372 --> 21:42.862
I swear I heard something.

21:44.009 --> 21:48.879
Adam, we have been over and
over this. There is nothing under your bed.

21:49.248 --> 21:54.186
There is nothing in the closet.
There are no such things as monsters.

21:54.855 --> 21:55.913
All right?

21:57.658 --> 21:59.820
- All right, I guess.
- Good.

22:00.729 --> 22:02.060
Now, try to go to sleep

22:02.163 --> 22:05.065
'cause we got to get up in the morning
and make movies.

22:05.167 --> 22:06.896
We're big Hollywood actors.

22:08.595 --> 22:09.721
Yeah, we are.

22:23.813 --> 22:26.247
This was exhausting.

22:26.416 --> 22:29.614
This whole experience
was absolutely exhausting.

22:29.720 --> 22:32.713
<i>You people have ruined
The Next Generation for me.</i>

22:32.824 --> 22:35.884
You are absolutely
the most insufferable group of jackasses

22:35.994 --> 22:39.522
I have ever had the misfortune of spending
an extended period of time with.

22:39.632 --> 22:41.293
I hope you all fucking die.

22:41.401 --> 22:43.597
I still have five prize tickets
from the carnival.

22:43.704 --> 22:46.434
There was nothing for five tickets.
We've been over this.

22:46.540 --> 22:50.443
Well, but LeVar and I were going to
pool ours for the fuzzy-troll pencil topper.

22:50.545 --> 22:51.808
Oh, yeah? You gonna share that?

22:51.914 --> 22:53.074
Yeah. We were gonna share it.

22:53.182 --> 22:54.240
Really? How was that gonna work?

22:54.350 --> 22:58.014
Three days at my house, three days
at LeVar's, and alternating Sundays.

22:58.121 --> 22:59.588
For a pencil topper?

22:59.690 --> 23:02.159
- I have to pee again.
- That's it. Goodbye.

23:03.461 --> 23:04.450
Fuck!

23:04.451 --> 24:05.451
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru